A||||8||RossT||dealer pricing (rip off)||||1||
Z||000000||RossT||12-01-2000||03:43 AM||||Well yesterday was the first time I went to the local pontiac dealer to check on a part for my fiero. My 88gt has the wheel locks and I decided to replace the 4 wheel locks with 4 regular LUG NUTS. I saw that the Fiero Store has them for $1.50 so I thought that the Pontiac dealer can't be much higher!<BR>WRONG. They wanted $7.43 each!!! Now that won't break me, but 7.43 for a lug nut!! <P> so iam off to the snow covered junk yard next chance.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||12-01-2000||04:20 AM||||Ross,<P>It sounds like the dealer made a mistake....they aren't really that much.  I have a bunch of lugnuts lying around.....I'll send you 4.||||reg||10
Z||000002||RossT||12-01-2000||04:25 AM||||Mike, I was thinking the same thing, so I called back several hours later, got some one else in the parts dept., had him look up the part, and got the same price. I could be<BR>a mistake on their computer I guess.<P>Thanks Mike.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||12-01-2000||04:29 AM||||I just e-mailed you about some T-Top parts.....I'll just give you the lugs if you need them.<P>The last time I priced the lugnuts they were in the $1.50-$1.75 apiece range (still too much!).  The ludicrous thing are those black plastic caps.....they're about $1.25 each!!! ||||reg||1
Z||000004||jmw||12-03-2000||05:06 PM||||If anybody needs those black plastic lug nut covers, Fiero Warehouse has a TON of them. Cheap. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tigger||12-03-2000||05:25 PM||||Someone not too long ago was looking for those black plastic caps.  The guy said a local dealer wanted $9 each for 'em.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||9
Z||000006||sqoach||12-03-2000||05:51 PM||||well hell, i just bought new lug nuts for all my wheels.  got 'em from o'reilly's. i don't have to worry about that stupid cap now.  i don't know if i still have those or not.<P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh<BR>fiero7@hotmail.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||12-03-2000||06:50 PM||||Whenever I need lugnuts or caps I just go wander around one of the local salvage yards. They are all over the place. I just take a 3/4 inch socket and a handle for the caps. much easier than messing with a lug wrench and won't score them up like pliers.<P>If you want new wheel locks get <A HREF="http://www.mcguard.com/" TARGET=_blank>McGard</A> at you local parts store. They are cheaper than the dealer. McGard are the only ones I'd use besides the OE ones. They have traditional ones as well as the kind that take the OE plastic covers. You may have to order the Fiero ones. Pep Boys at least doesn't have them on the rack.<P>I forget who makes the OE ones. If you call 1800PMCARES they can get you the phone number for the company that makes them.<P>I find the caps inconvenient but I like the look. If one gets lost or breaks they aren't hard to come up with replacement. I've seen chrome on the OE tech AL wheel. I didn't like them very much. My luck with chrome hasn't been very good. Even good one only take a certain amount of abuse before they look really bad.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 12-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||horseman||12-04-2000||12:21 AM||||My wheel lock tool says McGard on it. Looks like they made the OE ones. Does anyone have the black cover nut for the wheel lock? I am missing one and it is little larger than the stock lug covers.<BR>Charlie||||reg||1
